# Build context is the repo root (see Buildix.API/Dockerfile). Keep it lean and
# never ship local secrets or build output into an image layer.

# .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/

# Node / frontend build output (the web image builds its own dist)
**/node_modules/
Buildix.Web/dist/

# Git / IDE / OS
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.user

# Secrets — MUST never enter an image (mirrors .gitignore)
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
secrets.json

# Runtime data / docs / tests (not needed to build+run the API image)
Buildix.API/wwwroot/uploads/
docs/
**/*.md
deploy/
# ...bittasidan tashqari: web image runtime bosqichi shu skriptni ichiga oladi
# (sertifikat bo'lmasa vaqtinchalik o'zi imzolaganini yaratadi). Sertifikatlar
# va ACME holati esa YUQORIDAGI `deploy/` bilan tashqarida qoladi — ular hech
# qachon image ichiga tushmasligi kerak.
!deploy/nginx/ensure-cert.sh
